DESCRIPTION:Council meetings will be held either in person or remotely\, de
 pending on whether or not the Governor has declared a disaster emergency pu
 rsuant to the Governor's authority under Indiana Code Chapter 10-14-3. Ther
 e are two options\, described below:<br><p><b>Option 1:</b>&nbsp\;If the Go
 vernor declares or extends a disaster emergency through the date of this he
 aring as stated above\, the meeting will be held remotely and only remotely
  as allowed by Indiana Code5-14-1.5-3.7 and a Zoom link will be posted here
  at least a week before the meeting.</p><p><b>Option 2:</b>&nbsp\;If the Go
 vernor does not declare or extend a disaster emergency through the date of 
 this hearing as stated above\, a hybrid meeting will be held in a room in C
 ity Hall yet to be determined and also accessed via the Zoom link to be pos
 ted here&nbsp\;at least a week before the meeting.</p><br>Meetings of the C
 ommon Council are generally held the first four Wednesdays of the month at 
 6:30 pm\, in the Council Chambers (Suite 115\, City Hall\, 401 N. Morton).<
 br><br>For Council agendas\, legislation\, and all background material\, pl
 ease consult the Council's Legislative Packet posted on the Council's webpa
 ge under "Council Meetings:"&nbsp\;<a href="http://bloomington.in.gov/counc
 il">http://bloomington.in.gov/council</a><br><br>Questions? Please contact 
 the Council Office at 812.349.3409 or&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:council@bloomin
 gton.in.gov">council@bloomington.in.gov</a>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20230804T201818Z
