DESCRIPTION:<br>JOINT SESSION OF THE MONROE COUNTY COUNCIL\, MONROE COUNTY 
 BOARD OF COMMISSIONERS\, CITY OF BLOOMINGTON COMMON COUNCIL\, AND CITY OF B
 LOOMINGTON MAYOR.<br><br><br>TOPIC: THE CONVENTION CENTER PROJECT&nbsp\;<br
 ><br>&nbsp\; &nbsp\;---<br><br><i>Although not participating as a governing
  body at this meeting\, it is possible that a majority of the members of th
 e Monroe County Food &amp\; Beverage Advisory Commission may be also be pre
 sent this evening.  Since the gathering of a majority of that commission ma
 y be construed as a meeting of that governing body\, this statement also pr
 ovides notice of that eventuality.  Pursuant to Indiana Open Door Law (IC 5
 -14-1.5)\, this notice informs the public that this meeting will occur and 
 is open for the public to attend\, observe\, and record what transpires. </
 i><br><i><br></i><br><i>&nbsp\; &nbsp\;---</i><br><br><br>For Council agend
 as\, legislation\, and all background material\, please consult the Council
 's Legislative Packet posted on the Council's webpage under "Council Meetin
 gs:" <a href="http://bloomington.in.gov/council" id="ow1943" __is_owner="tr
 ue">http://bloomington.in.gov/council</a><br><br>Questions?  Please contact
  the Council Office at 812.349.3409 or <a href="mailto:council@bloomington.
 in.gov" id="ow1956" __is_owner="true">council@bloomington.in.gov</a><br><br
 >*Auxiliary aids for people with disabilities are available upon request wi
 th adequate notice. Please call 812.349.3409 or e-mail <a href="mailto:coun
 cil@bloomington.in.gov" id="ow1969" __is_owner="true">council@bloomington.i
 n.gov</a>.
