 hl3b5amhb50bc@group.calendar.google.com
CREATED:20240110T163721Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><b>This meeting will be held in the McCloskey Conference Roo
 m (Suite 135\, City Hall\, 401 N. Morton St) and may also be accessed elect
 ronically via Zoom (see information below).</b></p><p>Join Zoom Meeting<br>
 <a href="https://bloomington.zoom.us/j/84034009823?pwd=JX4aKcMsnt0B4DtdykHh
 wFbZl9OtzQ.1">https://bloomington.zoom.us/j/84034009823?pwd=JX4aKcMsnt0B4Dt
 dykHhwFbZl9OtzQ.1</a><br><br>Meeting ID: 840 3400 9823<br>Passcode: 409510<
 br><br>One tap mobile<br>+13052241968\,\,84034009823# US<br>+13092053325\,\
 ,84034009823# US<br><br>Dial by your location<br>• +1 312 626 6799 US (Chic
 ago)<br>Meeting ID: 840 3400 9823<br><br>Find your local number: <a href="h
 ttps://bloomington.zoom.us/u/kcyIl603EL">https://bloomington.zoom.us/u/kcyI
 l603EL</a><br></p><p>--</p><p>For Discussion:</p><p><b>In this meeting\, we
  will plan the Feb 25 panel discussion and discuss marketing. </b><br><br>E
 vent details as of 1/9/24:<br><br><b>Saturday\, February 24 at 4 - 6PM at I
 U Cinema</b> - a free\, ticketed screening of <i>Reimagining Safety</i>\, a
 n award-winning documentary about the problems of policing and alternative 
 solutions followed by 30-minute Q&amp\;A w film director moderated by IU's 
 Micol Siegel.<br><br><b>Sunday\, February 25 at 2 - 4:30PM at IU School of 
 Public Health\, Rm 125 (also on Zoom) </b>- a panel discussion entitled "Re
 imagining Safety in Bloomington" featuring in-person panelists film directo
 r Matthew Solomon\, Nick Voyles of Bloomington's Indiana Recovery Alliance\
 , Jordan McIntre of Bloomington's New Leaf New Life\, Amber Sherman a podca
 ster and Black liberationist of Memphis\, TN and Max Felker-Kantor of Ball 
 State. Possible (unconfirmed) online panelists will include national expert
 s from the film.<br></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240110T163842Z
LOCATION:City Hall-1-Cityhall McCloskey Conference Room (RM #135) (39)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Community Advisory on Public Safety Outreach Committee
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
