CREATED:20240920T192931Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><span>The Bloomington Common Council will hold a public hear
 ing at 6:30 P.M. on Tuesday October 1\, 2024 to consider local historic des
 ignation for:</span></p><p><span><span> </span></span></p><p><b><span>the G
 reen Acres Neighborhood in Bloomington\, IN\; bordered approximately by the
  </span></b><b><span>Illinois Central RR tracks\, State Road 46 bypass\, E 
 3<sup>rd</sup> Street\, N Union St\,and N Jefferson St (north of 7<sup>th</
 sup> St.)</span></b></p><p><b><span><span> </span></span></b></p><p><span>T
 he meeting will be conducted in a hybrid meeting format both electronically
  at the available link and in person at Bloomington City Hall\, City Counci
 l Chambers. The public may access the meeting at the following link:</span>
 </p><p><span><span> </span></span></p><p><u><span><a href="https://blooming
 ton.zoom.us/j/85081865702?pwd=R0WQgcqfCfUoSVgys2owWL83WE4TXZ.1" target="_bl
 ank">https://bloomington.zoom.us/j/85081865702?pwd=R0WQgcqfCfUoSVgys2owWL83
 WE4TXZ.1</a></span></u></p><p><u><span>Meeting ID: 850 81865702</span></u><
 /p><p><u><span>Passcode: 515113</span></u></p><p><u><span><span><span> </sp
 an></span></span></u></p><p><span>The hearing will be held for the purpose 
 of considering historic designation of the area as a Conservation District.
   </span></p><p><span><span> </span></span></p><p><span>Said hearing will b
 eheld in accordance with the provisions of Indiana Code 36-7-4-100 et. seq.
 \, the Bloomington Municipal Code\, and the Rules of the Bloomington Histor
 ic Preservation Commission.  All persons interested in this request may be 
 heard at the time and place as herein set out. You may also file written co
 mments with the Bloomington Historic Preservation Commission in the Departm
 ent of Housing and Neighborhood office\, where the petition is on file and 
 may be examined by interested persons. For questions concerning this matter
  or to submit electronic comments you may contact Noah Sandweiss at the Dep
 artment of Housing and Neighborhood Development (812)349-3420\; </span><spa
 n><span><a href="mailto:noah.sandweiss@bloomington.in.gov" target="_blank">
 noah.sandweiss@bloomington.in.gov</a></span></span><span>.</span></p><p><sp
 an><span> </span></span></p><p><span>Materials for Common Council considera
 tion will be available through this link: </span><span><span><a href="https
 ://bloomington.in.gov/council/meetings?year=2024" target="_blank">https://b
 loomington.in.gov/council/meetings?year=2024</a></span></span> </p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240930T152639Z
LOCATION:City Hall - Council Chambers\, 401 N Morton St\, Bloomington\, IN 
 47404\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Green Acres Historic District City Council Vote
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
