DESCRIPTION:INDOT to host public open houses for 2026-2030 Statewide Transp
 ortation Improvement Program (STIP) <br><table><tbody><tr><td><p>The Indian
 a Department of Transportation announces opportunities to learn more and pr
 ovide comments regarding its draft 2026-2030 Statewide Transportation Impro
 vement Program (STIP).   </p><p>The STIP is Indiana’s five-year planning an
 d construction document that lists all transportation projects expected to 
 be funded within the next five years using federal funding in addition to r
 egionally significant state funded projects. The current STIP (2024-2028) a
 nd draft 2026-2030 STIP are available on INDOT’s <a href="https://click.sub
 scription.in.gov/?qs=2ca9746f2d17469728e610d95d45738888b50955f3c72ff6d8e441
 01d2cd0bb3ac44bd4279b5b1f1f22b39296e315f06da000a58ec429f01877fa2f4c27e4fc0"
  target="_blank"><u>STIP webpage</u></a>. Learn more about the STIP with th
 e <a href="https://click.subscription.in.gov/?qs=2ca9746f2d17469744ff7ec0d8
 3830fa33ac304ab3e22526c55ee40cba69daae8d58a6249842c320a89a5065a1898158389b1
 b524ad2ada6008c9c5911825cd3" target="_blank"><u>STIP Public Primer</u></a>\
 , also available on INDOT’s STIP webpage.  STIP open houses will take place
  in 5 locations\, including <b>Bloomington. Bloomington's meeting will be h
 eld:</b><span> </span><span>Wednesday\, April 30\, 4-6 p.m.  in the City of
  </span><span>Bloomington City Hall Council Chambers (401 N Morton)\, from 
 4-6pm.  </span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><br>More information about the
  Indiana STIP can be found at: <br>~<a href="https://www.in.gov/indot/files
 /STIP_Primer.pdf" target="_blank">https://www.in.gov/indot/files/STIP_Prime
 r.pdf</a>\; <br>~<a href="https://www.in.gov/indot/resources/state-transpor
 tation-improvement-program-stip/" target="_blank">https://www.in.gov/indot/
 resources/state-transportation-improvement-program-stip/</a> <br>~<a href="
 https://www.in.gov/indot/resources/state-transportation-improvement-program
 -stip/stip-fy-2026-to-fy-2030/" target="_blank">https://www.in.gov/indot/re
 sources/state-transportation-improvement-program-stip/stip-fy-2026-to-fy-20
 30/</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250416T163215Z
LOCATION:City Hall-1-Cityhall Council Chambers (RM #115) (236)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Public Meeting for the Indiana Statewide Transportation Improvement
  Program (STIP)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
